1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,645
A message comes on your phone.

2
00:00:01,645 --> 00:00:03,344
Your credit card bill is ready.

3
00:00:03,863 --> 00:00:07,840
It shows two numbers. Total amount due,
thirty thousand rupees.

4
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:10,428
Minimum amount due, only fifteen hundred.

5
00:00:11,055 --> 00:00:12,950
Salary has not come yet.

6
00:00:12,950 --> 00:00:19,504
So you think, I will pay only the minimum,
right? No late fee. CIBIL score is safe.

7
00:00:19,504 --> 00:00:21,715
Many people think like this.

8
00:00:22,368 --> 00:00:23,609
But this is the real trap.

9
00:00:23,609 --> 00:00:26,282
ICICI Bank has put one example on its own
website. Look.

10
00:00:26,915 --> 00:00:31,508
One customer's bill was sixty nine
thousand, six hundred and eighty eight
rupees.

11
00:00:31,508 --> 00:00:34,683
On the last date, the customer paid sixty
five thousand.

12
00:00:34,683 --> 00:00:36,327
That is almost the full bill.

13
00:00:36,791 --> 00:00:39,773
But in the next bill, the bank added four
thousand,

14
00:00:39,773 --> 00:00:43,048
three hundred and seventeen rupees for
interest and GST.

15
00:00:43,471 --> 00:00:46,809
Only four thousand, six hundred and eighty
eight was not paid.

16
00:00:46,809 --> 00:00:49,071
But the interest was almost the same. How?

17
00:00:49,578 --> 00:00:54,397
By the end of this video, you will
understand the full maths behind that
small

18
00:00:54,397 --> 00:00:56,188
number. In very simple words.

19
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:59,270
Hello friends, welcome to Be Practical
with Kishore.

20
00:00:59,767 --> 00:01:01,092
First, the two numbers.

21
00:01:01,092 --> 00:01:04,722
Total amount due means the full money you
have to pay the bank.

22
00:01:05,062 --> 00:01:08,975
Minimum amount due is the small part you
must pay to not be late.

23
00:01:08,975 --> 00:01:13,128
Most banks keep it near five percent of
your bill, plus fees and GST.

24
00:01:13,486 --> 00:01:17,135
So for a thirty thousand bill, the minimum
is about fifteen hundred.

25
00:01:17,574 --> 00:01:20,551
Paying the minimum does two good things.
No late fee.

26
00:01:20,551 --> 00:01:23,360
And the bank will not report you as late
to CIBIL.

27
00:01:23,796 --> 00:01:25,729
But it does not stop interest.

28
00:01:25,729 --> 00:01:28,242
And you lose your interest free period.

29
00:01:28,610 --> 00:01:32,249
So remember this. The minimum amount is
not a safety net...

30
00:01:32,249 --> 00:01:35,086
it is a switch that starts the interest
meter.

31
00:01:35,469 --> 00:01:38,901
From the day you use your card till the
last date to pay,

32
00:01:38,901 --> 00:01:41,189
the bank does not charge any interest.

33
00:01:41,189 --> 00:01:43,898
This time is called the interest free
period.

34
00:01:43,898 --> 00:01:47,210
It simply means, for these days, you pay
zero interest.

35
00:01:47,624 --> 00:01:48,884
Let's take an example.

36
00:01:48,884 --> 00:01:51,348
On October fifth, ten thousand for a
phone.

37
00:01:51,348 --> 00:01:54,499
On the twelfth, fifteen thousand for a
family function.

38
00:01:54,499 --> 00:01:57,134
On the twentieth, five thousand for
groceries.

39
00:01:57,478 --> 00:01:59,860
On October twenty fifth, the bill comes.

40
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:01,229
Total, thirty thousand.

41
00:02:01,229 --> 00:02:03,492
Last date to pay, November fourteenth.

42
00:02:03,963 --> 00:02:06,652
So the phone money gets forty days
interest free.

43
00:02:06,652 --> 00:02:09,616
The grocery money gets twenty five days
interest free.

44
00:02:09,981 --> 00:02:11,445
But there is one condition.

45
00:02:11,811 --> 00:02:14,656
You must pay the full bill before the last
date.

46
00:02:14,656 --> 00:02:18,093
Even one rupee less, and the interest free
period is gone.

47
00:02:18,493 --> 00:02:19,885
This is in the RBI rules.

48
00:02:19,885 --> 00:02:21,667
If you do not pay the full bill,

49
00:02:21,667 --> 00:02:24,563
the bank can charge interest from the day
you spent.

50
00:02:25,012 --> 00:02:28,858
On November fourteenth, you paid only the
minimum, fifteen hundred.

51
00:02:28,858 --> 00:02:30,753
Now let's see what the bank does.

52
00:02:31,142 --> 00:02:34,711
Rule number one. Interest does not start
from the last date.

53
00:02:34,711 --> 00:02:37,268
It starts from the day you spent the
money.

54
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:41,434
On the ten thousand for the phone,
interest from October fifth.

55
00:02:41,434 --> 00:02:44,132
On the fifteen thousand, from October
twelfth.

56
00:02:44,132 --> 00:02:46,771
On the five thousand, from October
twentieth.

57
00:02:47,359 --> 00:02:53,013
How much interest? In banks like ICICI,
three point seven five percent every
month.

58
00:02:53,013 --> 00:02:55,533
That is forty five percent in a year.

59
00:02:55,988 --> 00:03:00,177
Rule number two. You pay interest even on
the money you already paid.

60
00:03:00,630 --> 00:03:04,138
Till November fourteenth, interest on the
full thirty thousand.

61
00:03:04,138 --> 00:03:08,035
Only after that, on the balance of twenty
eight thousand five hundred.

62
00:03:08,399 --> 00:03:12,470
Rule number three. On top of the interest,
eighteen percent GST.

63
00:03:12,935 --> 00:03:15,382
On November twenty fifth, the next bill
comes.

64
00:03:15,742 --> 00:03:17,270
You paid fifteen hundred.

65
00:03:17,270 --> 00:03:21,977
The bank added interest and GST of one
thousand, nine hundred and eighty one.

66
00:03:22,356 --> 00:03:24,701
So without spending even one new rupee,

67
00:03:24,701 --> 00:03:28,189
your bill went up from thirty thousand to
thirty thousand,

68
00:03:28,189 --> 00:03:29,873
four hundred and eighty one.

69
00:03:29,873 --> 00:03:32,519
You paid money, and still your loan went
up.

70
00:03:32,843 --> 00:03:34,311
This is our own maths.

71
00:03:34,311 --> 00:03:37,982
But we used the same method ICICI shows on
its website.

72
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:42,192
The same thing happened to the ICICI
customer we saw at the start.

73
00:03:42,192 --> 00:03:45,034
Interest on the full bill till the day of
payment.

74
00:03:45,034 --> 00:03:47,648
Then no interest free period for new
shopping.

75
00:03:47,648 --> 00:03:51,343
That is how it became four thousand, three
hundred and seventeen.

76
00:03:51,812 --> 00:03:56,188
Rule number four. Say on November
fifteenth, you fill petrol with the same
card.

77
00:03:56,188 --> 00:03:58,704
Will you get an interest free period for
that?

78
00:03:59,121 --> 00:03:59,317
No.

79
00:03:59,317 --> 00:04:04,672
Till the old bill is fully paid, every new
swipe gets interest from that same day.

80
00:04:04,965 --> 00:04:09,493
So from the day you paid only the minimum,
your card is not free any more.

81
00:04:09,493 --> 00:04:12,675
It has become a loan at forty five percent
interest.

82
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:16,505
Now, what if you pay only the minimum
every month?

83
00:04:16,977 --> 00:04:21,420
RBI rules say your loan should not grow if
you pay the minimum.

84
00:04:21,420 --> 00:04:23,324
So the loan does come down.

85
00:04:23,324 --> 00:04:24,875
But very, very slowly.

86
00:04:25,319 --> 00:04:28,807
In the first year, out of every hundred
rupees you pay,

87
00:04:28,807 --> 00:04:31,914
about seventy four rupees go to interest
and GST.

88
00:04:31,914 --> 00:04:34,260
Only twenty six rupees cut your loan.

89
00:04:34,671 --> 00:04:36,163
Start with thirty thousand.

90
00:04:36,163 --> 00:04:39,370
After one year, you would have paid about
twenty thousand.

91
00:04:39,370 --> 00:04:42,852
But about twenty four thousand, eight
hundred is still pending.

92
00:04:43,238 --> 00:04:46,372
After five years? You have paid about
seventy thousand.

93
00:04:46,372 --> 00:04:48,937
And still about thirteen thousand is
pending.

94
00:04:49,334 --> 00:04:52,213
To fully close it, it takes more than ten
years.

95
00:04:52,553 --> 00:04:56,368
That is why RBI makes banks print a
warning on every bill.

96
00:04:56,368 --> 00:05:00,314
If you pay only the minimum, you will keep
paying for years.

97
00:05:00,754 --> 00:05:04,616
India now has about eleven point eight six
crore credit cards.

98
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:09,935
As per CRIF High Mark, credit card bills
not paid for three months to one year were

99
00:05:09,935 --> 00:05:13,830
thirty three thousand, eight hundred and
eighty six crore rupees,

100
00:05:13,830 --> 00:05:15,508
in March twenty twenty five.

101
00:05:15,508 --> 00:05:18,685
That is forty four percent more than the
year before.

102
00:05:19,141 --> 00:05:21,387
Forty five percent is too much, right?

103
00:05:21,387 --> 00:05:23,456
But in December twenty twenty four,

104
00:05:23,456 --> 00:05:28,126
the Supreme Court cancelled an old order
that had put a thirty percent limit on

105
00:05:28,126 --> 00:05:31,613
credit card interest. So today, no court
has put any limit.

106
00:05:32,041 --> 00:05:34,755
So what saves you is not that small
number.

107
00:05:34,755 --> 00:05:36,333
It is knowing this maths.

108
00:05:36,688 --> 00:05:38,394
Some people use a shortcut.

109
00:05:38,394 --> 00:05:40,101
They call it card rotation.

110
00:05:40,514 --> 00:05:42,902
Take money from a friend and pay the full
bill.

111
00:05:42,902 --> 00:05:45,594
The next day, take the money out of the
card as rent,

112
00:05:45,594 --> 00:05:47,169
and give it back to the friend.

113
00:05:47,562 --> 00:05:50,747
But your loan does not come down even by
one rupee.

114
00:05:50,747 --> 00:05:54,369
Only the last date moves to next month.
And you pay a fee.

115
00:05:54,739 --> 00:05:59,191
Also, after new RBI rules in twenty twenty
five, apps like PhonePe,

116
00:05:59,191 --> 00:06:02,580
Paytm and CRED stopped rent payment by
credit card.

117
00:06:02,942 --> 00:06:05,740
Taking cash from your credit card is even
worse.

118
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:08,887
There is a fee, and interest starts from
the same day.

119
00:06:09,220 --> 00:06:11,075
So rotation is not a solution.

120
00:06:11,075 --> 00:06:13,425
It only pushes the loan to next month.

121
00:06:13,890 --> 00:06:16,613
So what should we do? Five simple steps.

122
00:06:16,963 --> 00:06:19,211
One. When you can, pay the full bill.

123
00:06:19,211 --> 00:06:23,161
If you set auto pay, set it for the full
amount, not the minimum.

124
00:06:23,469 --> 00:06:25,250
Then your card is really free.

125
00:06:25,250 --> 00:06:28,516
Up to fifty days interest free, depending
on your card.

126
00:06:28,902 --> 00:06:32,499
Two. If you cannot pay the full bill, pay
as much as you can.

127
00:06:32,499 --> 00:06:34,386
But never less than the minimum.

128
00:06:34,694 --> 00:06:37,629
Because interest on the money you pay
stops that day.

129
00:06:37,629 --> 00:06:39,622
Pay more, and you pay less interest.

130
00:06:39,622 --> 00:06:43,554
And once you clear the full bill, your
interest free period comes back.

131
00:06:44,011 --> 00:06:47,596
Three. Till the bill is cleared, keep that
card aside.

132
00:06:47,596 --> 00:06:50,451
Use UPI or a debit card for daily
spending.

133
00:06:50,849 --> 00:06:55,324
Four. If the bill is big, ask your bank to
change it into EMI.

134
00:06:55,324 --> 00:07:00,377
For example, HDFC's EMI rates are about
eleven to twenty five percent.

135
00:07:00,377 --> 00:07:02,326
Also check the fee and GST.

136
00:07:02,326 --> 00:07:05,141
And never take loans from unknown apps.

137
00:07:05,489 --> 00:07:05,796
Five.

138
00:07:05,796 --> 00:07:10,830
If your last date comes before your
salary, ask the bank to change your bill
date.

139
00:07:10,830 --> 00:07:13,592
RBI rules say they must give you this
option.

140
00:07:13,950 --> 00:07:18,442
One easy check. On your bill, look for the
line called finance charges.

141
00:07:18,442 --> 00:07:21,163
If it is not zero, you are paying
interest.

142
00:07:21,521 --> 00:07:26,230
Remember. The minimum amount saves you
from late fees and a bad CIBIL report.

143
00:07:26,230 --> 00:07:27,331
Not from interest.

144
00:07:27,675 --> 00:07:29,067
Remember three numbers.

145
00:07:29,067 --> 00:07:30,761
Forty five percent interest.

146
00:07:30,761 --> 00:07:32,456
Eighteen percent GST on top.

147
00:07:32,456 --> 00:07:36,934
And zero interest free days for new
spending till the old bill is cleared.

148
00:07:37,291 --> 00:07:39,843
The minimum is like an emergency brake.

149
00:07:39,843 --> 00:07:42,787
Use it only in an emergency, not every
month.

150
00:07:43,130 --> 00:07:44,604
What do you pay every month?

151
00:07:44,604 --> 00:07:46,184
The full bill, or the minimum?

152
00:07:46,184 --> 00:07:47,448
Tell me in the comments.

153
00:07:47,781 --> 00:07:52,074
In the next video, we will see what
happens if you cannot pay even the
minimum.

154
00:07:52,434 --> 00:07:56,130
If this helped you, share it with one
friend who uses a credit card.

155
00:07:56,130 --> 00:07:58,794
Subscribe to the channel. See you soon.
Jai Hind.

